Where did JSON come from?
JavaScript Object Notation
Why does it resemble Python dictionaries and lists?
Douglas Crockford specified and popularized JSON in the early 2000s for exchanging structured data between browsers and servers. It grew from JavaScript object syntax but is language-independent. response.json() parses JSON text into Python dictionaries, lists, and values. JSON’s rise belongs to the same Web 2.0 and API history as asynchronous browser interfaces.
