What should explanation do alongside code?
For each important result, document:

the question you asked;
the source and unit of observation;
the operation you performed;
what the output suggests;
what it cannot establish.


A notebook should not become a stack of unexplained cells. Markdown should preserve the researcher’s reasoning and make interpretive choices visible.
This connects directly to the final project. Students need to document not only what code ran, but why a particular operation represents their cultural question and what limitations remain.

